{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "A Brief History of HTML"}, {"type": "position", "content": 12}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear when people talk about HTML."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe common simple incidents at work in a simple spoken or written situation with a supportive interlocutor. Assess the incident of data in the macrosystem processes, based on the data dictionary to consolidate intervening data, based in established parameters."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation. Writes simple and short texts about programming tools and solutions to a client's requirement."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob12re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Search for the History of HTML."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Design a brochure in which you provide important facts about HTML and its History."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your product with your classmates."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I can recognize and list details from HTML History."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can summarize and demonstrate the evolution of HTML since its creation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can explain and discuss with my classmates facts about the development of HTML."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple past in statements and information questions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Use the simple past to talk about an action that finished in a specific moment in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">We can use&nbsp;<strong>past simple</strong> in affirmative sentences or in question form when we want to know some information about past events.&nbsp;</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Follow these structures to form affirmative statements and questions in past:&nbsp;<br /><br /><strong>Affirmative:</strong></p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">Subject + <strong>verb in past</strong> + complement.</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Example:</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><i>They <strong>created</strong> HTML to customize websites.</i></p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Interrogative:&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">Wh + <strong>did</strong> + subject + <strong>verb</strong> + complement +?</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Example:</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><i>When <strong>did</strong> they <strong>create</strong> HTML 5.0?</i></p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><i>Who <strong>made</strong> websites with HTML first?</i></p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Remember the purpose of each Wh question to use them correctly:</p>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p style=\\\"text-align: center;\\\"><strong>&nbsp;Wh question</strong></p>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p style=\\\"text-align: center;\\\"><strong>Refers to</strong></p>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Who\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a person\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"What\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a thing or an action\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"time\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Where\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a place\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Why\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"reason\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"How\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the way something was done\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm going to answer some questions we received in our blog this week."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Who created HTML?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Did HTML have a big impact on the web development world?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "It allowed designers to codify and publish documents with tables, pictures, video clips, sound clips, headings and texts."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "BODY "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "An HTML tag that defines a document's body"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Most of them controlled stylistic aspects of a document like the BGCOLOR attribute of the BODY element and FONT FACE."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob12aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "BGCOLOR "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an HTML attribute that specifies the background color of a document"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Most of them controlled stylistic aspects of a document like the BGCOLOR attribute of the BODY element and FONT FACE."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob12aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "frameset"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "kind of browser that only allows frame-related elements"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This version adopted many browser-specific element types and attributes, and more transitional and frameset."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob12aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "HTML5"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "latest version of the markup language HTML, used for structuring and presenting content on the World Wide Web "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: But, in 2014 they released HTML5 as the latest W3C recommendation."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob12aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "World Wide Web Consortium "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "(W3C) main international standards organization for the World Wide Web"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Later, the HTML 3.2 version resulted from the World Wide Web Consortium's (W3C) efforts to find a better version based on some of the users' needs."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob12aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "W3C Recommendation "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "standard at its highest level of maturation. It is endorsed by the W3C"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Then, in 1999 they published HTML.4,01 as a W3C recommendation and in 2001 they released their most improved version."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob12aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Identifying the main idea in a text"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you read a text, there are some things you have to take into account to understand the main idea."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>Firstly, you have to be clear with the reading objective. This means, to know whether you are reading to get an overview of the text, or if you want to look for a particular point.</p> <p>If you have to read the whole text, you need to focus on some key parts before you start with the details. For example, the introductory and the concluding parts, and also tables of contents and abstracts.</p> <p>Also, pay attention to the headings, because they usually have key ideas about the text content, and can guide you to key information.</p> <p>If the text has an index, it is important for you to check it and look for punctual information you may need.</p> <p>Look for words and phrases that link ideas; these will guide you to understand the connection of ideas in the text, and it will be easier for you to catch the main point in a short time.</p>"}], "type": "learning_points"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n2le02ob12re2aud01", "coverimg": "enpe8n2le02ob12re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n2le02ob12re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>HTML</strong></p>\n<p>To understand HTML we need to go over its history first. I&rsquo;m going to answer some questions we received in our blog this week.</p>\n<p><strong>Who created HTML</strong><strong>?</strong>&nbsp;While he was at CERN, Tim Berners-Lee developed the Hyper Text Markup Language, better known as HTML. It became popular thanks to Mosaic Browser, a browser developed at NCSA.<br /><br /><strong>Did HTML have a big impact on the web development world?</strong>&nbsp;Since its first appearance in the early 90's, it allowed designers to codify and publish documents with tables, pictures, video clips, sound clips, headings and texts. This language redirects information just by clicking a button on a webpage.</p>"}, {"time": "48000", "image": "enpe8n2le02ob12re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<p><strong>Did HTML change throughout the years?</strong>&nbsp;Yes, it did. In 1995, the IETF developed the HTML 2.0 to codify, a common practice in late 1994. In spite of not being a consensus regarding standard discussions, the drafts of HTML+ in 1993 and HTML 3.0 in 1995 led to new and richer versions of HTML. Later, the HTML 3.2 version resulted from the World Wide Web Consortium's (W3C) efforts to find a better version based on some of the users' needs.<br /><br /><strong>Was 1995 important for HTML history?</strong>&nbsp;Yes, of course. New HTML tags emerged during 1995. Most of them controlled stylistic aspects of a document like the BGCOLOR attribute of the BODY element and FONT FACE.</p>"}, {"time": "110000", "image": "enpe8n2le02ob12re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<p>In 1997, they released HTML 4.0. This version adopted many browser-specific element types and attributes, and more transitional and frameset. Then, in 1999 they published HTML.4,01 as a W3C recommendation and in 2001 they released their most improved version.&nbsp;<br /><br /><strong>Did HTML change again after that?</strong>&nbsp;For many years, new versions of HTML didn't appear. Through the early and mid-2000s, the W3C's HTML Working Group worked on the development of the XML-based language XHTML. But, in 2014 they released HTML5 as the latest W3C recommendation.</p>\n<p>Well, those were all the questions you asked on our blog, hope I was helpful. Don&rsquo;t forget to tune in for our next show.</p>"}]}, "type": "slideshow"}]}, {"_data": [], "title": "", "type": "video", "template_override": 1, "id": 2, "contents": [{"value": {"video_src": "enpe2n2le02ob12re5vsc01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "id": 0, "text": ""}]}, "type": "video"}]}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can understand written information about the history of HTML. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can read information about characteristi